ABOUT US

Capco is a global technology and management consultancy specializing in driving digital transformation in the financial services and insurance industries. Capco is committed to providing clients with practical solutions. We offer a globally integrated service with offices in leading financial centers across the globe. We have the people, the vision, and the passion.

We are growing through a significant growth journey, now is a very good time to join us as we expand geographically, increase headcount and disrupt the consulting market across APAC with entrepreneurial and agile thinking

&nbsp;

ROLE RESPONSIBILITIES

We are currently seeking a Senior Consultant to support and drive the growth of our Securities Services practice, with a strong focus on Custody Transformation. This is an exciting opportunity to be a leader, driving complex client programs, shape delivery approaches, and building consulting capability across the practice&nbsp;

As a Senior Consultant within the Securities Services team, you be part of Custody transformation projects across securities services for top-tier financial institution&nbsp;

&nbsp;

KEY RESPONSIBILITIES

• Work closely with business stakeholders, operations teams, product owners, and technology teams to deliver Custody transformation projects

• Gather, analyse, and document business requirements, user stories, process flows, and functional specifications across the custody operating model.

• Support change initiatives covering the end-to-end securities lifecycle, settlement, safekeeping, asset servicing, corporate actions, income processing, and reconciliation&nbsp;

• Conduct business process analysis and identify opportunities for operational efficiency, controls enhancement, automation, and digitization across custody operations&nbsp;

• Develop target operating models and future-state processes across custody and investor servicing functions.​‌

&nbsp;

KEY REQUIREMENTS

• 4+ years of experience within Global Custody, Securities Services, or financial services consulting&nbsp;

• Strong understanding of Custody and Securities Operation , including trade settlement, safekeeping, corporate actions, income processing, cash and securities, and asset servicing.&nbsp;

• Proven Business Analyst experience with requirements gathering, process mapping, gap analysis, functional documentation, and stakeholder management.

• Experience delivering change and transformation initiatives across custody platforms, securities servicing, or post-trade operations.&nbsp;

• Familiarity with&nbsp;SWIFT messaging, settlement processes, and market infrastructure such as Clearstream and Euroclear would be advantageous.&nbsp;

• Strong communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to engage business, operations, and technology teams.

• Immediately Available Preferred!

WHY JOIN CAPCO?

You will work on engaging projects with some of the largest banks and leading financial services in the world, on projects that will transform the financial services industry.

